2.2 Major changes made to the derived code
------------------------------------------

(a) Package and project identity
    All classes were re-packaged from `com.pvp_utils.*` to `com.yiyiaddon.ui.*`.
    The visible product name in the panel header was changed from "PVPUtils" to
    "yiyiaddon". No PVPUtils copyright or attribution notice was removed.

(b) Configuration backend
    PVPUtils reads and writes a single global `com.pvp_utils.Config` (Gson,
    persisted with `Config.save()`). yiyiaddon replaces it with a minimal
    configuration object, `com.yiyiaddon.config.AddonConfig`, backed by
    `config/yiyiaddon.json`. Only UI-related keys are carried over: panel theme,
    GUI scale, panel blur, blur strength, blur tint, scroll speed, GUI keybind
    and the Baritone localisation switch. No gameplay configuration was ported.

(c) Business content removed, replaced by UI test data
    Every PVPUtils ClickGUI page was removed and replaced by three pages that
    contain only UI verification data and never touch gameplay:
    `com.yiyiaddon.ui.page.TestPage`, `InterfacePage` and `SettingsPage`.
    Removed PVPUtils pages: CombatPage, RenderPage, ToolPage, OptimizePage,
    MiscPage, ThemePage (its theme/GUI portion was re-implemented as part of
    InterfacePage), AddServerPage and TermsScreen. `ResetManager` was not ported;
    the reset button now resets only yiyiaddon UI settings.

(d) Rendering entry point adapted to Minecraft 26.1.2
    PVPUtils targets Minecraft 1.21.11, where a screen draws through
    `render(GuiGraphics, int, int, float)`. Minecraft 26.1.2 replaced that model
    with an extract phase (`GuiGraphicsExtractor`). `SkiaScreen` was therefore
    rewritten: the extract phase only records mouse position and frame delta, and
    the actual Skija drawing is deferred to the end of the frame, where
    `com.yiyiaddon.mixin.client.RenderTargetMixin` injects at the head of
    `RenderTarget#blitToScreen` and calls `SkiaScreen#renderSkiaFrame`.

(e) Frame-cache path not ported
    PVPUtils ships a raster frame/region cache in
    `client/render/skia/SkiaRenderer.java`. That path depends on
    `GuiGraphics#blit` from 1.21.11, which does not exist in 26.1.2. It was not
    ported; the ClickGUI draws directly to the main framebuffer through
    `SkiaGlBackend` on every frame. Consequently the region content-hash hook
    (`SkiaRenderer.feedRegionContent`) was dropped from `FontRenderer`.

(f) Framebuffer handle lookup
    Both PVPUtils and yiyiaddon need the GL name of the main RenderTarget.
    PVPUtils reads it with `RenderSystem.getDevice() instanceof GlDevice`; in
    26.1.2 the GL backend is nested inside the GpuDevice wrapper. yiyiaddon
    reads it through the added `com.yiyiaddon.mixin.client.GpuDeviceAccessor`
    mixin and the `accessible class com/mojang/blaze3d/opengl/GlDevice` entry in
    `yiyiaddon.accesswidener`.

(g) Input method handling
    PVPUtils toggles Windows IME with JNA (`Imm32.ImmAssociateContext`) through
    its `InputMethodFix` module. That module is gameplay/optimisation code and
    was not ported. yiyiaddon uses the native 26.1.2 text-input API instead
    (`Minecraft#onTextInputFocusChange`, `Screen#preeditUpdated`), wrapped in
    `com.yiyiaddon.ui.render.ImeBridge`. IME pre-edit text is now drawn inline by
    `SettingTextBox`.

(h) Diagnostics and debug overlay removed
    The GPU diagnostic pixel read-back (`tracePresentedFramebuffer`,
    `captureMainFramebuffer`), the `Version.DEBUG` overlay and the
    `PVPUtils.LOGGER` calls were removed from the screen.

(i) Font resources
    Font files were moved from `/fonts/*.ttf` to
    `/assets/yiyiaddon/fonts/*.ttf`, which is the asset path required by the
    yiyiaddon mod id. The font files themselves are unchanged.

(j) Tab set
    The six PVPUtils sidebar tabs (Combat / Render / Tools / Optimize / Misc /
    Theme) were reduced to three (Test / Interface / Settings). Tab geometry,
    sidebar metrics, animation curves and control styling are unchanged.

(k) Theme registration left as-is
    PVPUtils registers only WhiteTheme, DarkTheme and GrayTheme in
    `ClickGuiThemeManager`. The remaining theme classes (LightBlueTheme,
    DefaultClickGuiTheme, VapeTheme) are also unregistered upstream. This was
    deliberately left unchanged: no visual redesign was performed in this phase.

